\maketitle

\section{Introduction}
Zimbabwe Sign Language (ISO 639-3 zib, Glottocode zimb1247) is the language of the Deaf community in Zimbabwe. It was recognised officially in the 2013 Constitution. Search results show policy and research literature but no dedicated dictionary or curriculum materials.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item NewsDay (2022) report on calls by the Deaf Zimbabwe Trust for a deaf syllabus and materials for Grade 4 to Form 4, and on a sign language syllabus workshop held in 2018: \url{https://newsday.co.zw/2022/01/provide-deaf-syllabus-to-ensure-equal-access-to-education-dzt}
\end{itemize}
No textbooks or signed curriculum materials were found.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Study of teachers implementing Zimbabwean sign language regulatory frameworks for deaf learners in special schools: \url{https://pubs.ufs.ac.za/index.php/ijsie/article/view/1289}
\item Sign language policies, practices and challenges in Zimbabwe's universities: \url{https://journals.udsm.ac.tz/index.php/jlle/article/view/4263}
\item The teaching and learning of sign language at the University of Zimbabwe: \url{https://eajess.ac.tz/?p=1966}
\item Deaf culture in Zimbabwe: existence, reality and implication for education: \url{https://opendocs.ids.ac.uk/opendocs/handle/123456789/6636}
\end{itemize}
No dictionary or grammar was found.

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item ZBC News on the University of Zimbabwe promoting sign language: \url{https://zbcnews.co.zw/featured/uz-promotes-sign-language-to-foster-inclusivity}
\end{itemize}
Deaf Zimbabwe Trust is named in the NewsDay report above. No website of its own was found.

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
No video corpus, signed dictionary or software was found.

\section{Curriculum Development Context}
Policy support exists (constitutional recognition, and a stated intention to teach sign language as a subject). Studies report that teachers lack training and teaching resources. A curriculum would need a signed dictionary and signed video materials, produced with Deaf community leadership.

\end{document}
